---
import Site from '../../../../layouts/Site.astro';
import OduSignature from '../../../../components/OduSignature.astro';
import {principalGuides} from '../../../../lib/principal-odu-guide';
import {oduLibrary,oduHref,type OduEntry} from '../../../../lib/odu-library';
export function getStaticPaths(){return oduLibrary.map(o=>({params:{slug:o.slug},props:{o}}));}
const {o}=Astro.props as {o:OduEntry};
const guide=o.principal?principalGuides[o.slug]:undefined;
const reverse=oduLibrary.find(x=>x.right.slug===o.left.slug&&x.left.slug===o.right.slug)!;
---
<Site title={o.name+' — Odù reference'} active="Learning">
<article class="wrap narrow article-section">
<p class="kicker">{o.principal?'PRINCIPAL ODÙ':'COMBINED ODÙ · COMPONENT LABEL'}</p>
<h1 lang="yo">{o.name}</h1>
<p><a href="/learning/ifa/odu/">← All 256 Odù</a></p>
<figure class="odu-display"><OduSignature right={o.right.code} left={o.left.code}/><figcaption>Left: {o.left.name} · Right: {o.right.name}</figcaption></figure>
<h2>Signature and structure</h2>
<dl class="glossary"><div><dt>Right column (first)</dt><dd>{o.right.name} · <code>{o.right.code}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Left column (second)</dt><dd>{o.left.name} · <code>{o.left.code}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Educational eight-bit encoding</dt><dd><code>{o.bits}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Decimal equivalent</dt><dd>{o.decimal} (not traditional seniority)</dd></div></dl>
<p>{o.principal?'Both columns match, forming a principal signature.':'The columns differ. Reversing their order gives a distinct configuration.'}</p>
{!o.principal&&<p><a href={oduHref(reverse.slug)}>Explore reversed pairing: {reverse.name}</a></p>}
{guide&&<section aria-labelledby="guide-title" class="principal-guide">
<h2 id="guide-title">Literary and philosophical introduction</h2>
<p class="notice"><strong>Editorial introduction based on the site owner's supplied material.</strong> The themes, narrative leads, name variants and associations below are awaiting specific source and practitioner review. They do not establish universal meanings or a lineage's reading.</p>
<h3>Names and introductory themes</h3><p lang="yo">{guide.aliases}</p><p>{guide.theme}</p>
<h3>Ìtàn — Narrative leads</h3><p>{guide.narrative}</p>
<h3>Ethical reflection</h3><p>{guide.reflection}</p>
<h3>Ire and Ibi — Contexts to investigate</h3><dl class="glossary"><div><dt>Ire</dt><dd>{guide.ire}</dd></div><div><dt>Ibi / Ayẹ̀wò</dt><dd>{guide.ibi}</dd></div></dl><p>These are themes from the supplied reference, not forecasts or outcomes assigned to a cast.</p>
<h3>Associated sacred figures and concepts</h3><p>{guide.associations}</p>
<h3>Ẹbọ and consultation</h3><p>Ritual prescriptions depend on the relevant verse, context and practitioner tradition. No fixed offering is assigned to this sign.</p>
<h3>Question for reflection</h3><p>How might the ethical reflection above apply to a real decision? What would a named practitioner or family tradition add or interpret differently?</p>
</section>}
<h2>Ẹsẹ Ifá — Oral literature</h2><p>{guide?'The supplied literary extracts and translations are retained in an editorial review register. They are not published here as authenticated verses because exact sources, context and permission remain unresolved.':'Attributed ẹsẹ Ifá, translations, traditional aliases and contextual interpretations are not yet available in this entry.'} No generic blessing, warning or prescription is assigned to this signature.</p>
<h2>Provenance</h2><p>Signature transcribed from the owner-supplied principal Odù tables. The combined pattern is generated from these component signatures. The reference has not yet been independently authenticated by a named practitioner or lineage.</p>
<p>Single = 1, double = 0 is our educational encoding. This page is not a personal reading.</p>
<p><a href="/learning/ifa/">Learn about Ifá readings and instruments</a> · <a href="/figures/orunmila/">Meet Ọ̀rúnmìlà</a></p>
</article>
</Site>
<style>.odu-display{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:1.5rem;margin:1rem 0;text-align:center}.odu-display :global(svg){max-width:180px}</style>
